WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:05.100
Marvel has a new crown jewel with the massively
popular and critically acclaimed Black Panther,

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.020
movie number 18 in the massive Marvel Cinematic
Universe.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.860
But if Wesley Snipes had gotten his way in
the 1990s, his cinematic take on the comic

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.120
would have pre-dated them all.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:19.060
The actor opened up to the Hollywood Reporter
in January 2018 about his experiences trying

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.740
and failing to get a Black Panther movie off
the ground.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.060
Here's why he says it never happened.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.100
Unshakable association

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.660
Snipes was first approached by Marvel for
a Black Panther adaptation in the early '90s,

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.020
when he'd just arrived as a major force in
Hollywood.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.280
He says it didn't take much convincing to
get him attracted to the project.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.920
"It had cultural significance, social significance.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:42.789
It was something that the black community
and the white community hadn't seen before."

00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:47.540
A major obstacle for Snipes and his collaborators
was name recognition, and what the words "Black

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:51.640
Panther" meant to the average film producer
in an era before comic book flicks were common.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:57.160
While the Black Panther character had existed
since 1966, so had the unrelated civil rights

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.960
organization with the same name: the Black
Panther Party.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.120
"(chanting)"

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.440
But the Black Panther character debuted months
before the group was formed, and has nothing

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.560
to do with the organization or its politics.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:15.510
The myth that they're linked has proven difficult
to shake over the years, and was at the root

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.680
of Snipes' troubles getting the project going.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.460
Director difficulties

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.640
Snipes brought the idea of a proudly Africa-centric
Black Panther movie to Boyz n the Hood director

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.980
John Singleton, one of a few directors considered
for the project, but ultimately hit a wall

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:33.020
when it came to Singleton's wildly differing
vision ... which centered on the Black Panther

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:33.520
Party.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:34.640
Snipes recalled,

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.780
"John wanted to take the character and put
him in the civil rights movement.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:38.540
And I'm like, 'Dude!

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:39.540
Where's the toys?!

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:43.670
They are highly technically advanced, and
it will be fantastic to see Africa in this

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.120
light opposed to how Africa is typically portrayed.'"

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:50.280
Singleton envisioned the film as a story about
a super-powered father butting heads with

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.680
his son over the politics of the Black Panther
Party.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:57.000
Ultimately, despite his disappointment, Snipes
says he's now able to see the benefit in parting

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:57.500
ways.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.540
"I love John, but I am so glad we didn't go
down that road.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:03.120
Because that would have been the wrong thing
to do with such a rich project."

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:04.620
Bad reputation

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.680
At the time, the Marvel brand had only been
used for a few movies — and they weren't

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:09.180
good.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.560
Marvel films of the era are notorious bombs.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:16.360
So it really says something that Snipes courted
the attention of some truly legitimate filmmakers

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.140
and screenwriters for Black Panther.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.880
But Snipes says that the timing just wasn't
right:

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.350
"Ultimately, we couldn’t find the right
combination of script and director and, also

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:29.411
at the time, we were so far ahead of the game
in the thinking, the technology wasn’t there

00:02:29.411 --> 00:02:31.860
to do what they had already created in the
comic book."

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:36.270
The 2018 adaptation, of course, doesn't share
that burden, with the slick realization of

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:40.440
Wakandan technology Snipes was hoping to bring
to the big screen way back in the early '90s.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.700
"But I have never seen anything like this."

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.140
"How much more are you hiding?"

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:46.440
Moving on

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:50.420
Though Snipes stayed dedicated to Black Panther
through the '90s, he eventually had to move

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:50.920
on.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:55.340
But he maintained his close relationship with
Marvel, and successfully kicked off a different,

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:58.420
darker superhero franchise with 1998's Blade.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:01.300
Snipes says the two characters are spiritually
related.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.720
"It was a natural progression and a readjustment.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:04.730
They both had nobility.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:05.720
They both were fighters.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:09.640
So I thought, hey, we can't do the King of
Wakanda and the vibranium and the hidden kingdom

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.520
in Africa, let's do a black vampire."

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.250
The movie's success would lead Marvel down
a path toward starting their own film studio

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.480
— and we all know what happened next.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.720
Far from bitter about his failed attempt at
making Black Panther, Snipes says he's thrilled

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.750
with this incarnation of the Wakandan king:

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:27.791
"Even though I am not a part of this particular
project, I support it 1000 percent, and I

00:03:27.791 --> 00:03:31.970
am absolutely convinced that it will be a
catalyst for change and open other doors and

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:32.840
other opportunities."

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.080
Thanks for watching!

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.420
